course: dictionary
lesson: 5042
title: Inky
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Inky is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like the fingers or the sky. It has two meanings: stained or covered with ink, and very dark, like ink.
explain: «Press an inky finger onto paper and you get a pattern of ridges.» The clues are press and paper. A finger that is pressed onto paper has been covered in ink, so inky means covered with ink here.
explain: «...all goes inky black.» Nothing is covered in ink here. The clues are thunder crashes and everything goes dark, so inky means very dark, like ink.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in a word that fits. If «very dark» still makes sense in the sentence, you have it right.
fact: Inky is an adjective, so it describes a noun: «inky fingers», «inky sky», «inky water».
fact: Inky can mean stained or covered with ink, like fingers after using a fountain pen.
fact: Inky can mean very dark, especially black or dark blue, like ink: «inky darkness».
fact: The comparative forms are inkier and inkiest.
exercise: «Press an inky finger onto paper and you get a pattern of ridges.» In this sentence, what does inky mean? | Very dark, like a night sky | Cold and hard | Wet from the rain | *Covered with ink
exercise: Lily says inky means wet. What does inky mean in «inky darkness»? | Covered in mud | *Very dark | Wet and cold | Loud and noisy
exercise: Find and copy the word that describes the fingers in «Her fingers were inky after the pen leaked.» | fingers | *inky | Her | leaked
test: «A black mamba opens its inky black mouth.» What does inky black mean here? | *Very dark black | Bright red | Pale grey | Soft and shiny
test: Ben says inky means happy. Why is he wrong? | Inky means happy and bright | Inky means small and round | Inky means very loud | *Inky means covered with ink or very dark, not happy
exam: Which word is the comparative of inky in «The night grew inkier as the storm came closer»? | inking | inkiest | inks | *inkier
